1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,567
The decision was made in a national convention hall, with a speaker who had come to follow the case to its end.

2
00:00:06,567 --> 00:00:12,926
“Who will handle our path?” a peasant from the intensive farming district asked.

3
00:00:12,926 --> 00:00:26,695
“A sentence in a document is not a road.” Perhaps the minister would come, and perhaps she would not; you could understand the room's mood from the empty seat in front.

4
00:00:26,695 --> 00:00:36,514
The abuse of privilege, the rejection of the due process, and the hostile rally outside were all part of the same small drama.

5
00:00:36,514 --> 00:00:52,762
“We may elect a council,” the speaker said, “or we may resist the whole convention.” They had to translate their preference into a policy, and the polish of the language did not make the choice easier.

6
00:00:52,762 --> 00:01:01,971
A sociable ambassador, a nationalist with a broad accent, and a container of harvest samples sat in the front row.

7
00:01:01,971 --> 00:01:20,089
“A privilege is derived from a duty,” she said, “and our duty is to the coast.” A kilogram of rice, a cushion on the chair, and a strap on a suitcase: the props of a formal argument about who belongs.

8
00:01:20,089 --> 00:01:27,923
The Olympics broadcast had been interrupted by the news; the war had killed the broadcast entirely.

9
00:01:27,923 --> 00:01:32,687
“Small children swim here in May,” a woman said.

10
00:01:32,687 --> 00:01:44,616
“Perhaps they will swim in September.” The infrastructure of the little resort had begun to drift, and no minister would take the toll on the road.

11
00:01:44,616 --> 00:01:54,800
The decision, when it came, was to originate a service rather than inherit one, and to worship nothing but the timetable itself.

12
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:08,943
“They will immigrate here for the speed,” the speaker said, “not for our sentiments.” It was late, the trains had stopped, and the work of the next year was already written on the board.

13
00:02:08,943 --> 00:02:13,303
The regard of the country had become a job in itself.

14
00:02:13,303 --> 00:02:35,357
“The fact is,” the speaker said, “that a national hall can hold a thousand people and still miss the small stop where you get off.” A broad path, a due process, and a preference for the harvest over the rally: the decision would follow the facts, not the crowd.
